{
 "_readme": "Shared contract for FullTextResult.jats_xml, FullTextResult.pdf_download_failure and FullTextResult.tier_faults: the service hands back the JATS it rendered, byte for byte as served, and the cache keeps it beside the HTML; a PDF tier whose download leaves no file says why (#594); a result carries the faults the tiers before it swallowed (#603). bmlib's Python (tests/test_fulltext_source_contract.py) and Rust (rust/bmlib/tests/fulltext_source_contract.rs) assert against this file. Each case runs fetch_fulltext against a transport answering `responses` in order; `body_file` names a file in tests/fixtures. `jats_xml` names the body_file the result must carry exactly, or null. `seed_html` writes an HTML entry with no XML beside it before the call, as a bmlib that predates jats/ left it; `seed_unreadable_jats` then puts a directory where its XML entry belongs, which cannot be read, and `moved_aside` says that entry is under a .corrupt suffix after the call. An answer carrying `raise` fails as a transport error instead of answering. `seed_pdfs_dir_as_file` puts a file where the cache's pdfs/ directory belongs, so no PDF can be saved. `pdf_download_failure` is the cause the result must carry (absent: null) and `pdf_cached` whether it carries a `file_path` (absent: false). `tier_faults` is the fault type names the result must carry, in order (absent: none). A case expecting `raises` makes fetch_fulltext fail instead of returning: `exhausted` says whether the error is the typed exhaustion error (Python FullTextExhaustedError, Rust FullTextError::Exhausted, #565), and for one, `faults` and `absences` are what it carries. `then` repeats the request once the responses are spent, so it can only be answered from the cache. `fetch_pdf_with_jats` builds the service with that option on and no wait between retries (#739, #744); `doi` is passed as the request's DOI; `then_responses` answers the `then` lookup in order (absent: none), so a cached JATS hit whose PDF is sought again (#744) can be answered. Expected values are hand-written, never generated by the code under test.",
